# Licenses and data provenance

## Package: LPPL 1.3c or later

Copyright Anar Abdullayev. The azhyphen software, TeX/Lua runtime, maintenance
tool, tests, generated hyphenation patterns and package documentation are
distributed under the LaTeX Project Public License version 1.3c or, at your
option, any later version. Full terms: LPPL-1.3c.txt.

Maintenance status: maintained. Current Maintainer: Anar Abdullayev.
Reports: https://github.com/abdanar/azhyphen/issues.

The five runtime files are azhyphen.sty, azhyphen.lua, azhyphen.pat.txt,
azhyphen-xetex.tex and azhyphen-version.tex. Derived patterns and metadata
are part of the maintained package. No third-party pattern dataset is used.

## Word lists: CC0 1.0 Universal

To the extent possible under law, Anar Abdullayev waives all copyright and
related or neighboring rights in data/hyphenated.txt and data/evaluation.txt
under CC0 1.0 Universal. These lists may be reused, corrected, extended and
redistributed, including in other hyphenation projects. Full terms:
CC0-1.0.txt and https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/.
This separate grant was explicitly authorized by the maintainer on
2026-10-13; it does not place the software or generated patterns under CC0.
Future data contributions must be offered under the same CC0 terms.

## Migration provenance

The 2,270 annotations were migrated on 2026-10-13 from the maintainer's
original annotation project: its current training list (2,007 words) became
data/hyphenated.txt and its separate evaluation list (263 words) became
data/evaluation.txt. Both lists match the original annotated gold data and
the split used for the bundled model. Their order, characters and hyphen
positions were preserved; only CRLF line endings were normalized if present.

The original annotation application required human acceptance or editing
before saving suggestions from the maintainer's rule engine. Its provenance
records describe 2,211 accepted suggestions, 9 corrected suggestions and
50 earlier manual annotations. Review of the source history, annotation
workflow and these lists found no third-party annotation import or restrictive
notice. Only the reusable annotated words were migrated: no unannotated
dictionary, application, metadata, personal information, backups or history.
The maintainer's express CC0 grant covers these annotations; no rights in
other material from that project are asserted here.

The previous exported patterns had an LPPL grant dated 2026-10-07. Their
generator reused historical patterns as input, so that exact 291-pattern
snapshot was not derivable from the word lists and final parameters alone.
The self-contained generator preserves that recipe and annotations but
starts from empty patterns, producing a fresh reproducible model. Current
quality is measured solely from the public evaluation data and generated
patterns, and displayed in README's generated block. The public datasets
and this repository's Git history now provide the source history; building
requires no external checkout, export, commit identifier or private path.
